  "created": "2026-11-11T19:20:15.563Z",
  "description": "Winnovative Next HTML to PDF Converter for .NET (Linux ARM64) is a core component of the Winnovative PDF Next Library for .NET, using an advanced and reliable Chromium-based rendering engine that processes modern HTML, CSS and JavaScript content to the latest standards.\n\nThe converter targets .NET Standard 2.0 and can be used in .NET Core and .NET Framework applications deployed on Windows, Linux and macOS, including Azure, AWS, Google Cloud, Docker and Kubernetes.\n\nThis package installs only the Linux ARM64 runtime. For Linux x64, the package Winnovative.Pdf.Next.HtmlToPdf.Linux can be referenced on its own or alongside this package.\n\nSeparate packages are available for Windows, macOS or multi-platform runtimes.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* Linux (ARM64) - Debian 11+, Ubuntu 20.04+ or equivalent\n* .NET 11.0, 10.0, 9.0, 8.0, 7.0, 6.0 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* AWS Elastic Beanstalk and AWS Lambda on Graviton\n* Linux Virtual Machines\n* Docker containers and Kubernetes for Linux\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert HTML with CSS, web fonts and JavaScript to PDF\n* Support modern web standards and technologies\n* Generate PDF/UA and PDF/A compliant documents\n* Add HTML with page numbers in headers, footers and stamps\n* Repeat HTML table headers and footers in PDF pages\n* Control PDF page breaks with CSS in HTML\n* Create outlines and tables of contents from heading tags\n* Convert HTML forms to interactive PDF forms\n* Convert or exclude specific HTML regions\n* Retrieve HTML element positions in the PDF\n* Trigger conversion automatically or manually\n* Render for screen or print media\n* Set PDF security, viewer settings and signatures\n* Set HTTP headers and cookies\n* Use GET and POST requests\n* Convert HTML to images\n* Convert SVG to PDF\n* Asynchronous methods for async/await\n\nDocumentation and code samples:\nhttps://www.winnovative-software.com/winnovative-pdf-next-html-to-pdf-dotnet",
